704 The number of spiders is 90. The number of millipedes is 1/3 of the number of spiders, so we calculate 1/3 * 90 = 30 millipedes. The number of stink bugs is twice the number of millipedes minus 12, so we calculate 2 * 30 - 12 = 60 - 12 = 48 stink bugs. The total number of bugs is the sum of the number of spiders, millipedes, and stink bugs: 90 + 30 + 48 = 168.

90 spiders + 30 millipede + 48 stink bugs = 168 bugs

So, the total number of bugs Nancy counted is 168. \boxed{168}
